From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] ui: the headroom the guest tone-maps into, tested without AppKit

What: a header with no AppKit in it: the HDR headroom QEMU gives the guest
(the window's display's EDR headroom now, at least 1 = SDR white, at most
the display's potential and 16) and when a new value goes out (the first
one, PQ starting or stopping, a move of 10 % or more). Used by
omacvm-cocoa-hdr-headroom.patch (which explains the why; ADR 0048).

Why its own file: so the rules are tested without QEMU or a window
(app/runtime/Tests/display/test-hdr-headroom.sh applies this patch to an
empty folder; at build time and in CI).

Upstream: OmacVM only (QEMU has no way to tell a guest a display's
headroom; this goes over OmacVM's display port).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-hdr-headroom.c.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/ui/omacvm-edr.h
@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+/*
+ * OmacVM, HDR (ADR 0048): the headroom QEMU gives the guest to tone-map
+ * into. No AppKit in here, so it is tested on its own
+ * (app/runtime/Tests/display/test-edr.c); ui/cocoa.m feeds it NSScreen's
+ * values.
+ *
+ * macOS shows the guest's PQ frames without tone-mapping them again (the
+ * layer's toneMapMode is never), so the guest must keep its highlights
+ * within what the panel can show now: its EDR headroom (1.0 = SDR white,
+ * PQ 203 nits). The headroom follows the panel's brightness; a look once a
+ * second sends a new value only when it moved by 10 % or more.
+ */
+#ifndef OMACVM_EDR_H
+#define OMACVM_EDR_H
+
+#include <math.h>
+#include <stdbool.h>
+
+/* The most the guest is given: 16 x 203 nits, past every Mac panel's peak. */
+#define OMACVM_EDR_MAX 16.0
+
+/*
+ * The headroom for the guest from the window's display: its current EDR
+ * headroom (or, with use_potential, its most), at least 1 (SDR), at most
+ * the display's potential and OMACVM_EDR_MAX, in 1/100 steps.
+ */
+static inline double omacvm_edr_value(double current, double potential, bool use_potential)
+{
+    double v = use_potential ? potential : current;
+
+    if (!isfinite(v) || v < 1.0) {
+        v = 1.0;
+    }
+    if (isfinite(potential) && potential >= 1.0 && v > potential) {
+        v = potential;
+    }
+    if (v > OMACVM_EDR_MAX) {
+        v = OMACVM_EDR_MAX;
+    }
+    return round(v * 100.0) / 100.0;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Whether a new value goes to the guest: the first one, PQ starting or
+ * stopping (0 = PQ cannot be shown), or a move of 10 % or more. now < 0
+ * (HDR not wanted) never goes out.
+ */
+static inline bool omacvm_edr_moved(double sent, double now)
+{
+    if (now < 0) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    if (sent < 0) {
+        return true;
+    }
+    if ((sent == 0) != (now == 0)) {
+        return true;
+    }
+    if (sent == 0) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    return fabs(now - sent) >= 0.10 * sent - 1e-9;
+}
+
+#endif
